@page "/"

<PageTitle>Flirty Designer</PageTitle>

<h1>Flirty Designer</h1>

<p>
    Welcome to the Flirty designer. Here you configure dialogs and manage the database connections.
</p>

<p>
    First create a connection profile under <a href="connections">Connections</a>, migrate it and
    activate it. After that you manage everything else under <a href="dialogs">Dialogs</a>:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Create, edit, publish, unpublish and delete <strong>dialogs</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Questions</strong> with answer options, question type and validation rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Transitions</strong> (branching) with live-checked conditions.</li>
    <li>Mark <strong>loops</strong> over the existing back-jump.</li>
    <li><strong>Triggers</strong> as back channels into the host application (in-process or webhook).</li>
    <li><strong>Test run</strong>: play the dialog through with the real engine – even as a draft.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    A <strong>published</strong> dialog is locked, so that running sessions do not break.
    To evolve it, the dialog editor creates a <strong>new version</strong> as a draft.
</p>
